        "id": 83537,
        "name": "jagarciao",
        "username": "jagarciao",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jagarciao/{size}/2010_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-12-04T17:14:40.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I have a deck available for each hero and their promo version and have used them together with varying degrees of success using a variety of house rules.&nbsp;</p><p>Free-flowing beer and fun-loving friends certainly increase the chances of success/fun.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>P.S. I have mentioned this before, but I'll reiterate: if you are going to use multiple decks of the same hero in one game I recommend you mark the cards for one deck or sleeve them differently or somehow differentiate them in some way (I put a small blue dot on the corner of one deck). Otherwise you might spend a lot of time separating the decks if you mix them/drop them accidentally.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:06:39.087Z",
