      {
        "id": 83538,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-12-04T17:39:09.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It has been said that there is only one Legacy at a time, and that makes sense, because there is only one ring, and the bearer is Legacy.</p><p>So for multiple Bunkers, or Legacies or whatever to happen you would need time shiftiness.</p><p>If you have time shiftiness, which the most recent expansion was sort of all about, then any freedom 6 promos could easily repeat, Tachyon and TL Tachyon teaming up to save their friend from himself (or at least trying),</p><p>For others, Wraith going back in time to stop RC Wraith from making a terrible mistake, or to stop a villain from going back and killing her or something. &nbsp;Eternal Haka somehow getting his younger self, and trying to fix some terrible wrong that would change history.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I know Pauline goes out with her dad and the team, but she wouldn't be leading them, and a good chunk of the deck reflects the leadership aspect of Legacy. &nbsp;With timelines converging it would make sense to use that deck, since you could get each Legacy when they were Legacy.</p><p>I'd want a modified deck to reflect Pauline before she inherited the ring, one that was less leadership and less dominant, maybe more focused on damage or having a minor role on the team.</p><p>I just couldn't put the Legacy deck out there for Pauline while her dad was still in charge.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
